  "non_claims": [
    "PKSCHED1 is a fixed-capacity foundation and does not close the complete N12 scheduler phase.",
    "The live machine-code proof runs cooperatively on the BSP; no application processor executes a scheduled task.",
    "No interrupt, timer, wakeup, or remote IPI preemption path is installed or claimed.",
    "The two live tasks remain in one kernel address space with one unchanged CR3; ring 3 and process address-space switching remain open.",
    "The live tasks deliberately avoid x87, SSE, AVX, debug-register, and PMU state; full extended-state switching remains open.",
    "FS base, GS base, and kernel GS base are observed unchanged rather than assigned per task.",
    "The one-lock direct inheritance model is not chained inheritance, deadlock detection, lockdep, futex, condition-variable, or general sleeping-lock support.",
    "The raw spinlock has bounded acquisition and misuse detection but is not yet an IRQ-save, NMI-safe, queued, or production-contention implementation.",
    "The Python oracle checks a deterministic overlapping trace; it is not a proof of all Rust executions.",
    "The predecessor TLA model has three tasks, one CPU context, and no liveness claim; full implementation refinement remains open.",
    "No topology-aware balancing, hotplug, NUMA, SMT policy, tickless idle, scheduler watchdog, latency target, or PDC policy hook is implemented.",
